# pool_house -- generated by tools/cad/build_shells.py from tools/cad/shells/. DO NOT EDIT.
# pool house: 9 x 5, a true 3-arch colonnade on the front, low hip roof behind a parapet
# 10.0 x 6.0 m footprint, 4.7 m tall. One piece per material group, all at the
# building's own origin: `tex NAME TILE` is per model file, so a wall and a roof cannot
# share one. The y on each line is the height that group was drawn at, put back: model.c
# rebases every OBJ's lowest vertex to zero, which would otherwise land the roof on the
# ground. Hand-placed extras, if any, follow at the bottom from
# tools/cad/shells/extras/pool_house.part
piece models/own/shell/pool_house_floor.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.730 1.910 2.200  tex paving_stone 0.5
piece models/own/shell/pool_house_wall.obj   0 0.200 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.570 1.740 2.390  tex plaster_cream 0.5
piece models/own/shell/pool_house_trim.obj   0 2.350 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/shell/pool_house_roof.obj   0 3.600 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.420 1.530 1.970  tex roof_tile 1.2

# The kit's frames, seated IN the reveals the shell cuts: each piece is pushed back
# into the wall by its own architrave projection, so the moulding finishes flush with
# the plaster instead of standing on it. Generated from the same Walls calls that cut
# the holes, so a frame and its reveal cannot drift apart.
piece models/own/arch/plain_door.obj   -0.000 0.200 2.440   1.000 1.000 1.000   180.0 0.0 0.0   1.470 1.250 0.880  tex planks_weathered 2.5
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   -4.437 1.120 -0.000   0.900 0.900 0.900   90.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   4.437 1.120 0.000   0.900 0.900 0.900   -90.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/pool_house.part ----
# Hand-placed, not part of the shell's fabric: the two teak benches under the outer arches,
# kept from the original hand-built pool_house.part.
piece models/shapes/box.obj -3.0 0.2 -2.3 1.2 0.4 0.4 0 0 0 1.47 1.25 0.88 tex planks_weathered 2.5
piece models/shapes/box.obj 3.0 0.2 -2.3 1.2 0.4 0.4 0 0 0 1.47 1.25 0.88 tex planks_weathered 2.5

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/pool_house_facade.part ----
# Carried from the hand-authored arch/pool_house_facade.part this replaces: the cornice below
# the parapet, all four walls, at the wall top (y 3.6) -- unchanged, since the footprint and
# wall height it rides on did not change.
#
# The old balustrade that used to ride above the front cornice (y 3.95) is NOT carried across:
# the shell now builds a real, solid parapet on all four sides with shelllib.parapet(), per the
# brief's must-have list, and a decorative balustrade line buried inside that solid coping would
# be wasted geometry rather than a railing you could see. Flag this if a balustrade-topped
# parapet was actually wanted instead of a solid one.
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj     0.000  3.600  -2.500   9.000 1.000 1.000    0.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj     0.000  3.600   2.500   9.000 1.000 1.000  180.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj     4.500  3.600   0.000   5.000 1.000 1.000  270.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj    -4.500  3.600   0.000   5.000 1.000 1.000   90.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
